## Target Identity and Functional Architecture

The axis is literal cedar-vetiver tailoring: Virginia cedar and target Haitian vetiver are more audible, while Iso E, Vertofix, Azarbre, Hedione, violet green, and sandalwood keep the grain supple. Pencil shavings, smoke, and generic dry amberwood pressure fail the name. TARGET / IDEAL remains separate in `../candidates/LH-08.json`.

## Current-Inventory Build — Heuristic Volume Adapter

The shared child core is 4,200 µL and the controlled module is exactly 300 µL. Indian volume-grade vetiver maps—but cannot establish—Haitian identity.

